<title>ITALY: Italy excludes Swiss, Hong Kong from tax reform.</title>
<headline>Italy excludes Swiss, Hong Kong from tax reform.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy has excluded investors from Switzerland and Hong Kong from a reform abolishing withholding tax on Italian government bonds and paper for foreigners, a list published in the Official State Bulletin on Friday said.</p>
<p>The reforms are set to be introduced on January 1, 1997 and will cover Italian government bonds and paper including BOTs, BTPs aand CCTs.</p>
<p>Some 67 countries will be covered by the changes, including vitrually all major European countries, Russia, the United States, Mexico, China and Singapore. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
